Cobalt Harbor performed an offline incident readiness review for questionnaire evidence log s009230 on 2026-07-20. The evidence question was: Which source fact would cause the reviewer to accept the control conclusion? The response coordinator assembled the source facts; the case reviewer tested their independent confirmation. The review relates AC-27 to evidence set 184 and records RISK-031 as the governing risk reference. Dependency context: no upstream dependency. The source record is p03-src-009230 and this artifact is p03-full-009230. The evidence instrument was the recertification record; the reviewer observed that the exception route was visible to an independent reviewer. During challenge, a policy reference was checked against the operating record. Review profile: the evidence set was collected before the approval meeting; the evidence custodian confirmed the record boundary; the reviewer sampled an adverse operating condition; the source fact supported acceptance with a documented caveat; the comparison used the prior review conclusion; the evidence was retained in the review register; the exception path was not invoked; the reviewer found no handover impact; the decision was suitable for routine monitoring; the source chronology was complete; the control claim was corroborated by a compensating observation; the review boundary excluded unavailable material; the next assurance trigger is the scheduled review; the disposition was communicated to the independent reviewer; the retained rationale supports repeat review; the record remains a local offline assurance artifact. Counterexample considered: A single approval cannot settle a conflicting record; the discrepancy must remain visible to the reviewer. Decision rule: Escalate conflicting observations to the designated reviewer rather than resolving them through filename or identifier changes. Disposition: escalated for corroboration with the decision basis retained. No Kio capability is used or required for